From: knulli
Subject: [PATCH] celt/arm: vroundf must use the fallback on 32-bit ARMv8 with GCC

vcvtaq_s32_f32 is AArch64-only in GCC.  Its arm_neon.h for AArch32 ships
only the __fp16 vcvta variants (vcvtaq_s16_f16), so an ARMv8 board built
in 32-bit mode fails with "implicit declaration of vcvtaq_s32_f32".
clang does provide it for A32, which is presumably why the guard reads
__ARM_ARCH >= 8.

vminvf() and vmaxvf() just below already guard on __aarch64__ alone; make
vroundf() match.  The fallback is plain NEON and works everywhere.

--- a/celt/arm/mathops_arm.h
+++ b/celt/arm/mathops_arm.h
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 
 static inline int32x4_t vroundf(float32x4_t x)
 {
-#  if defined(__aarch64__) || (defined(__ARM_ARCH) && __ARM_ARCH >= 8)
+#  if defined(__aarch64__)
     return vcvtaq_s32_f32(x);
 #  else
     uint32x4_t sign = vandq_u32(vreinterpretq_u32_f32(x), vdupq_n_u32(0x80000000));
